        "Immanuel Bloch",
        "Markus Greiner",
        "Peter Zoller"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Ultracold atoms in optical lattices made controlled quantum many-body systems experimentally accessible, enabling direct study of phenomena that are otherwise difficult to isolate.",
        "attribution": "Bloch and Greiner led landmark experimental demonstrations, while Zoller helped establish the theoretical framework; Cirac and Esslinger also made substantial contributions.",
        "maturity": "The platform has been reproduced and extended by many groups and has yielded durable results across quantum many-body physics.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "A prize limited to three people would leave out major theoretical and experimental contributions."
        ]
      }
    },
