        "Denis J. Evans",
        "Gavin E. Crooks"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Fluctuation theorems and exact work relations sharpened the foundations of nonequilibrium statistical mechanics and connected microscopic reversibility to measurable macroscopic behavior.",
        "attribution": "Evans, Jarzynski, and Crooks made distinct, influential contributions to the theory; the broader intellectual history of nonequilibrium thermodynamics also matters.",
        "maturity": "The relations are well established and have been tested in experiments, including small systems where fluctuations can be measured directly.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The field's conceptual importance is clear, but the breadth of impact beyond statistical physics may be judged differently by the committee."
        ]
      }
    },
